       Given the page is loaded
       When I type "   " into the new-todo input
       And I press Enter
       Then the todo list contains 0 items
  6) Input is focused on page load # features/todo-core.feature:42
       Given the page is loaded
       Then the new-todo input has focus
  7) Toggle a todo as completed # features/todo-core.feature:47
       Given the page is loaded
       Given I create a todo with text "Read a book"
       When I click the toggle checkbox for "Read a book"
       Then the item "Read a book" has class "completed"
       And the toggle checkbox for "Read a book" is checked
  8) Toggle a completed todo back to active # features/todo-core.feature:53
       Given the page is loaded
       Given I create a todo with text "Read a book"
       And I click the toggle checkbox for "Read a book"
       When I click the toggle checkbox for "Read a book"
       Then the item "Read a book" does not have class "completed"
       And the toggle checkbox for "Read a book" is not checked
  9) Remove a todo by clicking the destroy button # features/todo-core.feature:62
       Given the page is loaded
       Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
       When I click the destroy button for "Buy milk"
       Then the todo list contains 0 items
  10) Counter shows remaining items count # features/todo-core.feature:69
       Given the page is loaded
       Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
       And I create a todo with text "Walk dog"
       And I create a todo with text "Read"
       And I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy milk"
       Then the todo-count text is "2 items left"
  11) Counter pluralization for single item # features/todo-core.feature:76
       Given the page is loaded
       Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
       Then the todo-count text is "1 item left"
  12) Counter pluralization for zero items # features/todo-core.feature:80
       Given the page is loaded
       Given the todo list is empty
       Then the todo-count text is "0 items left"
  13) Clear completed removes all completed todos # features/todo-core.feature:86
       Given the page is loaded
       Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
       And I create a todo with text "Walk dog"
       And I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy milk"
       When I click "Clear completed"
       Then the todo list contains 1 item
       And the remaining item has title "Walk dog"
  14) Clear completed button is hidden when no completed todos exist # features/todo-core.feature:94
       Given the page is loaded
       Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
       Then the clear-completed button is not visible
  15) Clear completed button is shown when completed todos exist # features/todo-core.feature:98
       Given the page is loaded
       Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
       And I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy milk"
       Then the clear-completed button is visible
  16) Double-clicking a todo label enters edit mode # features/todo-editing.feature:12
       Given the page is loaded
       And I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
       When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
       Then the item "Buy milk" has class "editing"
       And the edit input for "Buy milk" is focused
       And the edit input for "Buy milk" contains "Buy milk"
  17) Edit is saved when the edit input loses focus # features/todo-editing.feature:20
       Given the page is loaded
       And I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
       When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
       And I change the edit input to "Buy oat milk"
       And the edit input loses focus
       Then the todo list contains 1 item
       And the item "Buy oat milk" does not have class "editing"
       And the item "Buy milk" does not exist
  18) Edit is saved when Enter is pressed # features/todo-editing.feature:30
       Given the page is loaded
       And I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
       When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
       And I change the edit input to "Buy oat milk"
       And I press Enter in the edit input
       Then the todo list contains 1 item
       And the item "Buy oat milk" does not have class "editing"
  19) Edit input is trimmed before saving # features/todo-editing.feature:39
       Given the page is loaded
       And I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
       When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
       And I change the edit input to "   Buy oat milk   "
       And I press Enter in the edit input
       Then the todo list contains 1 item
       And the remaining item has title "Buy oat milk"
  20) Empty edit destroys the todo # features/todo-editing.feature:48
       Given the page is loaded
       And I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
       When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
       And I change the edit input to ""
       And I press Enter in the edit input
       Then the todo list contains 0 items
  21) Whitespace-only edit destroys the todo # features/todo-editing.feature:54
       Given the page is loaded
       And I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
       When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
       And I change the edit input to "   "
       And I press Enter in the edit input
       Then the todo list contains 0 items
  22) Escape key discards the edit and restores original title # features/todo-editing.feature:62
       Given the page is loaded
       And I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
       When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
       And I change the edit input to "Buy oat milk"
       And I press Escape in the edit input
       Then the edit input for "Buy milk" is not visible
       And the item "Buy milk" does not have class "editing"
       And the item "Buy milk" has title "Buy milk"
  23) Creating a todo persists it to localStorage # features/todo-persistence.feature:11
       Given the page is loaded
       When I type "Buy milk" into the new-todo input
       And I press Enter
       Then localStorage contains a todo with title "Buy milk" and completed false
  24) Toggling a todo persists the completed state # features/todo-persistence.feature:16
       Given the page is loaded
       Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
       When I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy milk"
       Then localStorage contains a todo with title "Buy milk" and completed true
  25) Deleting a todo removes it from localStorage # features/todo-persistence.feature:21
       Given the page is loaded
       Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
       When I click the destroy button for "Buy milk"
       Then localStorage does not contain a todo with title "Buy milk"
  26) Editing a todo persists the new title # features/todo-persistence.feature:26
       Given the page is loaded
       Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
       When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
       And I change the edit input to "Buy oat milk"
       And I press Enter in the edit input
       Then localStorage contains a todo with title "Buy oat milk" and completed false
       And localStorage does not contain a todo with title "Buy milk"
  27) Uses the correct localStorage key # features/todo-persistence.feature:36
       Given the page is loaded
       Given the page is loaded
       Then localStorage has a key starting with "todos-"
  28) Todos are restored from localStorage on page load # features/todo-persistence.feature:42
       Given the page is loaded
       Given localStorage has a stored todo with title "Buy milk" and completed false
       When the page is reloaded
       Then the todo list contains 1 item
       And the new item has title "Buy milk"
       And the new item is not completed
  29) Editing mode is not persisted # features/todo-persistence.feature:49
       Given the page is loaded
       Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
       When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
       And I change the edit input to "Buy oat milk"
       And the page is reloaded
       Then the item "Buy milk" does not have class "editing"
  30) All todos are shown by default # features/todo-routing.feature:11
       Given the page is loaded
       Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
       And I create a todo with text "Walk dog"
       And I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy milk"
       And the route is "#/"
       Then the todo list contains 2 items
  31) Active filter shows only uncompleted todos # features/todo-routing.feature:20
       Given the page is loaded
       Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
       And I create a todo with text "Walk dog"
       And I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy milk"
       When the route is "#/active"
       Then the todo list contains 1 item
       And the remaining item has title "Walk dog"
  32) Completed filter shows only completed todos # features/todo-routing.feature:30
       Given the page is loaded
       Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
       And I create a todo with text "Walk dog"
       And I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy milk"
       When the route is "#/completed"
       Then the todo list contains 1 item
       And the remaining item has title "Buy milk"
       And the remaining item is completed
